      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T10:09:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This method can only make mNextExpirationTime smaller; but it is possible that it gets larger here, if this method updated a service to extend the expiration time\n\nShould this just be mNextExpirationTime \u003d getNextExpirationTime() ?\n\nIf you were using \"mNextExpirationCheckTime\" (e.g. the next time to check, which can be \u003c\u003d the next actual expiration as I suggested in the previous review) it would work, but in that case you wouldn\u0027t need to calculate getNextExpirationTime; you could just use the expiration time of the added service, since that\u0027s the only service that may have a shorter expiration time than before.\n\nBut here since you\u0027re doing the whole calculation of the exact next expiration time, it can just be used as-is.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 196,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "16283cb051503271ea751d2764138909b9eeaea8",
