      "message": "A comment to explain why this would not be updated if it is higher than the current expiration time would be useful\n\nBut actually I think you might not want to use this. I think you\u0027ve got 2 options:\n - Use mNextExpirationCheckTime, and document it to be \"less than or equal to the lowest expiration time of the services\". Then only update it when adding a service (using min(mNextExpirationCheckTime, newServiceExpirationTime)) or after calling removeExpiredServices\n - Or recalculate the exact expiration time every time you add, update or remove a service",
